  "worked_solution": "We can evaluate this limit in terms of the constant $c$ using direct substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{5}^{x}+c}{{2}^{x}-1} & =\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to 1}({5}^{x}+c)}{{lim}_{x\\to 1}({2}^{x}-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{5}^{1}+c}{{2}^{1}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5+c}{2-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5+c}{1} \\\\  & =5+c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the above limit is equal to $4,$ we can equate the above with $4,$ and then solve for $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5+c & =4 \\\\ c & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
